 "notes": "Official TwoLayerModel (model_twolayer.py) with the README/__main__ configuration (input_len=100, patch_len=25, feature_dim=512, ResMLP x6, expansion=2, dropout=0.2, reg=MeanMLP x3, GELU), unchanged (out_dim=3, dims=3 as in the tlio card). The IPB input (B,6,200) @200 Hz is first decimated by a parameter-free 2-tap average (avg_pool1d k=2 s=2) to (B,6,100), i.e. the 1 s @100 Hz input stated in the official README comment. Channel order [gyro, acc] is kept (the official repo ships no data pipeline; TLIO order is [gyro, acc]). Outputs: displacement = out_linear(512->3) (vel = displacement / 0.995 s in the IPB wrapper), logstd = out2_linear(512->3) (log-sigma semantics inherited from TLIO, not verifiable in this repo). numpy>=2 needs sys.modules stubs for numpy.lib.arraypad/arraysetops imported (unused) by model_MLP.py.",
